cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MediClaimPilot or its technical report, please cite it as below."
title: "MediClaimPilot: A Multi-Agent LLM System for Auditing US Medical Bills and Drafting Patient Disputes"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Anamika
    family-names: Bajpai
version: 1.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24535521
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Melody5star/mediclaimpilot"
abstract: >-
  MediClaimPilot is an open-source system that splits US medical bill review
  into six agents (parser, bill auditor, denial analyzer, strategy agent,
  document writer and deadline tracker). It flags charges worth questioning
  using CMS Medicare fee schedule rates and LLM review, decodes denial codes,
  and drafts dispute letters for human review. The accompanying technical
  report documents the design, one real-world case study and the system's
  limitations.
keywords:
  - medical billing
  - LLM agents
  - multi-agent systems
  - healthcare
  - patient advocacy
